<misterromdescription>
    <name>Poker Dice (v1.7)</name>
    <setname>pokrdice</setname>
    <rbf>Gm0rk_ITech8</rbf>
    <mameversion>0289</mameversion>
    <mratimestamp>20261004</mratimestamp>
    <year>1991</year>
    <manufacturer>Strata / Incredible Technologies</manufacturer>
    <category>Casino / Dice</category>
    <players>1</players>
    <joystick>none</joystick>
    <rotation>vertical (cw)</rotation>
    <num_buttons>7</num_buttons>
    <buttons names="Play,Raise,Upper Left,Upper Right,Middle,Lower Left,Lower Right,Coin,Service" default="Start,B,X,Y,A,L,R,Select"/>

    <romstruct>
Board select (ioctl index 1): 0B = itech8 6809 board (3), 64 KB program
(bit 3); second byte 85 = MAME's lo memory map (bit 0), one 8-bit page
display (bits 2-1 = 2), YM2203 sound board, vertical, turned clockwise
(bit 7, MAME ROT90); third byte 03 = Poker Dice's inputs.
Download stream (ioctl index 0), 1,146,880 bytes:
000000 - 007FFF   32K  sound program                  -> block RAM
008000 - 017FFF   64K  main program                   -> SDRAM bank 0
018000 - 057FFF  256K  OKI samples region (64K used)  -> SDRAM bank 2
058000 - 117FFF  768K  graphics ROM region (256K used)-> SDRAM bank 1
    </romstruct>

    <rom index="1">
        <part>0B 85 03</part>
    </rom>

    <rom index="0" zip="pokrdice.zip" md5="63cbd6ee4abe30063e61ab7fa9190e7e">
        <!-- sound program (sound CPU $8000-$FFFF) -->
        <part name="pd-snd.u27" crc="4925401c"/>
        <!-- main program (64 KB: banks at $4000, last 32 KB at $8000) -->
        <part name="pd-v1.7_u5.u5" crc="5e24be82"/>
        <!-- OKI M6295 samples -->
        <part name="pd-srom0.srom0" crc="f85dbd6f"/>
        <part repeat="0x30000">00</part>
        <!-- graphics ROMs -->
        <part name="pd-grom0.grom0" crc="7c2573e7"/>
        <part name="pd-grom1.grom1" crc="e7c06aeb"/>
        <part repeat="0x80000">00</part>
    </rom>

    <!-- 8 KB battery-backed RAM (CPU $2000-$3FFF) -->
    <nvram index="4" size="8192"/>
</misterromdescription>
